# /etc/packmoat/packmoat.env: the server's settings. Root-only, mode 600. Caddy must never read this file.
# Every setting the server reads is listed here. docs/self-hosting.md explains each one, and how to read one from a file instead.
# After a change, recreate the container:  docker compose -f /opt/packmoat/deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d --force-recreate packmoat

# ---- Required
# The master key, from: docker run --rm --entrypoint packmoat-admin packmoat:local keygen
PACKMOAT_MASTER_KEY=
# The feed host names, separated by spaces. Not the admin or customer site host.
PACKMOAT_HOSTS=packages.contoso.example
# The database file inside the container. The image already sets this; change it only if you know why.
# PACKMOAT_DB=/data/packmoat.db
# The database engine: exactly sqlite or postgres (lowercase, no spaces). Unset: sqlite. Only sqlite works today: postgres, or any
# other value, stops both the server and packmoat-admin.
# PACKMOAT_DB_ENGINE=sqlite

# ---- Optional: the feed
# The public address of the feed, if something in front of Caddy hides it. Unset: the request's own host is used.
# PACKMOAT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://packages.contoso.example
# Requests per token per minute before the feed answers 429. Unset: 6000.
# PACKMOAT_TOKEN_RPM=6000
# Reverse proxies, besides one on this machine, that may pass on the client's address: IP addresses or networks, separated by spaces.
# Unset: loopback only, which is right for the Caddy in this kit. Never 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 (refused).
# PACKMOAT_TRUSTED_PROXIES=10.0.0.0/8
# The daily retention pass: on or off. Unset: on. Off only for a second copy of the server on the same database (then run
# packmoat-admin jobs run retention daily, or keep it on in one copy).
# PACKMOAT_BACKGROUND_JOBS=on

# ---- Optional: the operator admin site (unset PACKMOAT_ADMIN_HOST: no admin site)
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_HOST=admin.contoso.example
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_TENANT_ID=
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID=
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Who may sign in: directory id and user object id pairs, tid:oid, separated by commas. Empty: nobody.
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_ALLOW=
# Unset: the admin-keys folder next to the database (/data/admin-keys).
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_KEYS_DIR=
# Where the cookie keys live: folder (the key folder above; unset means folder) or database (encrypted with the master key, shared by
# every copy of the server on one database; the first start copies the folder's keys in once). Anything else stops the server.
# PACKMOAT_COOKIE_KEYS=folder
# Unset: pkgs.dev.azure.com.
# PACKMOAT_ADMIN_UPSTREAM_HOSTS=pkgs.dev.azure.com

# ---- Optional: the customer site (unset PACKMOAT_APP_HOST: no customer site)
# PACKMOAT_APP_HOST=app.contoso.example
# PACKMOAT_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# PACKMOAT_APP_CERT=/data/app-signin.pem
# The Azure setup wizard: off, on, or directory GUIDs separated by commas. Unset: off.
# PACKMOAT_AZURE_SETUP=off

# ---- Optional: who runs this server, as the customer pages name you
# PACKMOAT_OPERATOR_NAME=Contoso IT
# PACKMOAT_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@contoso.example
# PACKMOAT_SITE_URL=https://contoso.example
